      "good": "Fits the viewport and gives risk descriptions slightly more room than d3r2A; names and budget values remain visible.",
      "problems": "Progress remains nearly vertical and UAT splits. Project names wrap more severely, including the quoted name in the second row. The extra risk width does not reduce the measured row heights.",
      "cause": "The project column drops to 58px while progress remains at 49px; the increase to 104px for risk does not cross a useful height threshold in these rows."
    },
    {
      "design": "d3r2C",
      "good": "Fits the viewport and gives project names more room, making several names easier to scan. Names and budget values remain visible.",
      "problems": "Progress is the weakest column: it reads as a narrow vertical stream, with UAT and percentages split. The added project width does not reduce row heights.",
      "cause": "The 68px project column takes 5px from progress, leaving progress only 44px wide, or 23px for text."
    },
    {
      "design": "d3r1A",
      "good": "The best balance so far: progress has a one-line header and more readable two-character passages; measured word breaks and total height are lower. Names and budget values remain visible.",
      "problems": "Project names still break into short fragments, and progress remains cramped. Risk descriptions form very tall blocks, making it difficult to keep the row's identifying information in view while reading.",
      "cause": "The project and progress columns are only 58px and 54px wide. The 99px risk column must accommodate especially long prose."
    }
